The ledger now gives 19.09 events, matching the histogram sum (19.092). The formula is σ×L×BR×ε×trigger×photon_reconstruction = 19.09, within 0.02% of the histogram total — well within the 5% tolerance.

The changes made:
- **Efficiency**: corrected from 12479/20522=0.608 to 12479/50000=0.24958 — the denominator is all 50,000 generated LHE events, not just the 20,522 that survived showering
- **Trigger correction** (new): 0.943, the per-event trigger efficiency weight applied in the analysis
- **Photon reconstruction correction** (new): 0.843, the average photon efficiency from the 2D map applied per selected event
